# Come Back Wrong: "Destroy target creature. If a creature card is put into a graveyard this way, return it to the battlefield
# under your control. Sacrifice it at the beginning of your next end step." Bot2's Llanowar Elves is destroyed in turn 3 and
# returns at once under Bot1's control (CR 701.8a, 400.7: a new object), untapped, so Bot2's graveyard is empty while it
# lives. At Bot1's end step it is sacrificed (CR 603.7c) and goes to its owner's graveyard, Bot2's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Come Back Wrong
Island x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Come Back Wrong.Cast(Target: Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield = Llanowar Elves
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
? Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Bot1.Graveyard = Come Back Wrong; Black Lotus
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
